## Part (b): $\alpha(r)\sin 7\theta$ at $z=0$

This is part (a) with only the $n=7$ sine mode: $b_7(r) = \alpha(r)$, all others zero.

$$\boxed{u(r,\theta,z) = \sum_{m=1}^{\infty} B_{7m}\,J_7\!\left(\frac{j_{7,m}\,r}{a}\right)\sinh\!\left(\frac{j_{7,m}(H-z)}{a}\right)\sin(7\theta)}$$

with

$$B_{7m} = \frac{2}{a^2\,J_8^2(j_{7,m})\,\sinh(j_{7,m}H/a)}\int_0^a \alpha(r)\,J_7\!\left(\frac{j_{7,m}\,r}{a}\right) r\,dr.$$

